nvme: advertise FLUSH/FUA on the namespace queue

The 3.10 NVMe driver (v0.8) handles REQ_FLUSH and REQ_FUA bios
(nvme_submit_bio_queue) but never calls blk_queue_flush(), so the block
layer strips every flush before it reaches the driver
(block/blk-core.c "Filter flush bio's early"). fsync() then completes at
the SSD's volatile write cache: measured 0.24 ms per 8KB dsync write
without this change, 2.77 ms with it, on a Samsung SM961-class SSD
behind a Synology M2D18 in a DS1517+ (DSM 7.2-72806, kernel 3.10.108).
A database on the unpatched driver can lose committed data on power loss.

--- a/drivers/block/nvme-core.c
+++ b/drivers/block/nvme-core.c
@@ -1576,6 +1576,7 @@
 	queue_flag_set_unlocked(QUEUE_FLAG_NOMERGES, ns->queue);
 	queue_flag_set_unlocked(QUEUE_FLAG_NONROT, ns->queue);
 	blk_queue_make_request(ns->queue, nvme_make_request);
+	blk_queue_flush(ns->queue, REQ_FLUSH | REQ_FUA);
 	ns->dev = dev;
 	ns->queue->queuedata = ns;
 
